{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ESiYjBz5pXgpbjuvXrwhYE","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","edits":[{"oldText":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets - sum the count from all rows\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.count())\n\n# Filter census to get US total (usually marked with specific code or name)\n# First, let's see the structure and get the total population\ncensus_total = census.aggregate(total_population=census.max())\n\n# Simple join: both are aggregates so we cross-join\nresult = markets_total.join(census_total, how='cross')\n\n# Calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = result.mutate(\n    markets_per_100k=(result.total_markets / result.total_population * 100000)\n)","newText":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets - sum the farmers_markets column\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Filter census to get US total and extract population for 2025\ncensus_us = census.filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\ncensus_total = census_us.select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Cross-join (Cartesian product) to combine the aggregates\nresult = markets_total.join(census_total, how='cross')\n\n# Calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = result.mutate(\n    markets_per_100k=(result.total_markets / result.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n)"}]}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that the census data has a row for \"United States\" with the name in the NAME column. The current population estimate for 2025 is in the POPESTIMATE2025 column, which shows 341,784,857.\n\nNow I can write the build script properly:\n1. Read farmers markets - sum the `farmers_markets` column\n2. Read census - get the row where NAME == \"United States\" and get POPESTIMATE2025\n3. Calculate the ratio per 100,000\n\nLet me update the build script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the structure. Let me update the build script to properly aggregate the data:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ESiYjBz5pXgpbjuvXrwhYE","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","edits":[{"oldText":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets - sum the count from all rows\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.count())\n\n# Filter census to get US total (usually marked with specific code or name)\n# First, let's see the structure and get the total population\ncensus_total = census.aggregate(total_population=census.max())\n\n# Simple join: both are aggregates so we cross-join\nresult = markets_total.join(census_total, how='cross')\n\n# Calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = result.mutate(\n    markets_per_100k=(result.total_markets / result.total_population * 100000)\n)","newText":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets - sum the farmers_markets column\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Filter census to get US total and extract population for 2025\ncensus_us = census.filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\ncensus_total = census_us.select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Cross-join (Cartesian product) to combine the aggregates\nresult = markets_total.join(census_total, how='cross')\n\n# Calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = result.mutate(\n    markets_per_100k=(result.total_markets / result.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n)"}]}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":1163,"cacheRead":9927,"cacheWrite":4516,"totalTokens":15619,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.005815000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0009927,"cacheWrite":0.005645,"total":0.0124657},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":128},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914526806,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77RhGxygFFLeryNVLsR","rawStopReason":"tool_use"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"toolu_01ESiYjBz5pXgpbjuvXrwhYE","toolName":"edit","args":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","edits":[{"oldText":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets - sum the count from all rows\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.count())\n\n# Filter census to get US total (usually marked with specific code or name)\n# First, let's see the structure and get the total population\ncensus_total = census.aggregate(total_population=census.max())\n\n# Simple join: both are aggregates so we cross-join\nresult = markets_total.join(census_total, how='cross')\n\n# Calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = result.mutate(\n    markets_per_100k=(result.total_markets / result.total_population * 100000)\n)","newText":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    xo.get_connection(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\n        \"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36\"\n    })\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets - sum the farmers_markets column\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Filter census to get US total and extract population for 2025\ncensus_us = census.filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\ncensus_total = census_us.select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Cross-join (Cartesian product) to combine the aggregates\nresult = markets_total.join(census_total, how='cross')\n\n# Calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = result.mutate(\n    markets_per_100k=(result.total_markets / result.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n)"}]}}
